DESCRIPTION:Home of SF’s #1 Espressotini!Balboa Cafe’s Balboa Block Pa
 rty returns October 18 at Greenwich and Fillmore in San Francisco. The str
 eet fundraiser supports the PlumpJack Foundation and is promoted with espr
 essotinis and community gathering.\nSince 1913\, Balboa Cafe has served as
  one of San Francisco’s oldest restaurant where it all started as a work
 ing-man’s saloon. Now it’s a cherished neighborhood establishment wher
 e people from all corners of the Bay Area and beyond come for community an
 d our beloved classics\, like the Balboa Burger on a baguette\, the Wednes
 day Chicken Paillard special\, and the famed Espressotini. Despite our cit
 y’s evolution\, Balboa Cafe remains a timeless destination for those see
 king a taste of San Francisco’s nostalgia.\nWe don’t know the exact de
 tails for 2026 but we expect it to be similar to 2025. Here’s last year
 ’s details for reference until we have specifics for 2026.\n\n2025 Detai
 ls for reference\nSunday\, October 19\, 2025 • 1 PM – 7 PM\nOverview\n
 Music\, Food\, Drinks & Fun for a good cause: The PlumpJack Foundation\nBa
 lboa Cafe’s annual celebration and fundraiser for the PlumpJack Foundati
 on features our signature smash burgers\, espressotini’s on tap (plus ot
 her beverages)\, and a full line-up of music to get you groovin’ in the 
 streets.\nMusic Line-Up\nMonkey 1pm-3pm\nMitch Polzak & the Royal Deuces 3
 pm-5pm\nChris Clouse Project – Headliner_\nOriginal Event Description:\n
 _You heard it here first! Balboa Block Party is back on Sunday\, October 1
 8th at Greenwich...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com/p/DdWzeh
 vCTxS/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&amp\;stkn=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==\nDetails: ht
 tps://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-balboa-block-party-2026-greenwichfillmore/\nSour
