SUMMARY:Essential Oil + Tea Blending Workshop for the Fall Season
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T153000
DTSTAMP:20261019T210249Z
UID:dothebay-17955879@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Food & Drink
DESCRIPTION:Join herbalist and multidisciplinary healer Allie Brown for an
  herbal crafting workshop\, encouraging you to slow down and tend to your 
 own garden. Craft a custom herbal tea infusion and aromatherapy essential 
 oil blend. Experience the synergy of a sound\, guided meditation\, scent\,
  and summer inspired herbal tea infusions. Learn how to utilize the sacred
  energetics of scent and herbs to celebrate the vibrant energy of the fall
  season.\n\nThrough hands-on herbal medicine making and guided reflection\
 , you'll explore the Metal element. In traditional Chinese medicine\, fall
  is connected to the lungs and large intestine. This makes fall a season f
 or tending to grief\, inner reflection\, and letting go.\n\nWe'll discuss 
 the properties and energetics of herbs such as ginger\, cinnamon\, and blu
 e butterfly pea-plants known for their ability to warm the body\, enhance 
 intuition\, soothe the nervous system\, and boost immunity. Tea infusions 
 are made from herbs and other plant materials (e.g.\, flowers\, roots\, st
 ems\, fruit\, etc.) and lead to a medicinal benefit for the body. Learn ab
 out essential oils-such as bergamot and frankincense-for grounding your bo
 dy.\n\nAllie will lead a guided meditation and acupressure session with va
 rious sound healing instruments. Your oil blend and massaging self-touch w
 ill serve as a peaceful salve to an overactive nervous system.\n\n$55-$75.
 \n\nPresented by Gardens of Golden Gate Park\n\n$55-$75.\nGardens of Golde
 n Gate Park\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/essential-o
 il-tea-blending-workshop-for-the-fall-season-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
