 arbor Days\nOur October edition lands a week before Halloween\, so the mus
 ic has a spooky streak this month. Jugglers wander the waterfront\, ferrie
 s pull in from the city\, and more than 60 vendors set up along the Ferry 
 Landing.\n\nFrom noon to 3\, a costumed face painter turns kids into butte
 rflies\, tigers and whatever else they can dream up\, at no cost. Nearby\,
  the Children’s Experience Station has hula hoops\, ribbons and juggling
  props for anyone who wants to give them a go\, parents included.\nMake a 
 day of it. Downtown Sausalito is right across the street\, so grab lunch o
 n Bridgeway\, duck into a gallery or two\, and wander the shops before hea
 ding home.\nEvent details\n\nSaturday\, October 24\n10 AM – 3 PM\nSausal
 ito Ferry Landing\nFree admission\n\n@sausalitoartandharbordays\n\nFree\n\
