BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Bread History Talk\, Tasting & Guided Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T130000
DTSTAMP:20261021T115902Z
UID:funcheap-1640638@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerAndrew CoePlease join us on Sa
 turday\, October 24\, 2026 for an extraordinary in-person opportunity to h
 ear Andrew Coe speak about the history of American bread\, while sampling 
 a variety of historically important breads.\nWhy did supermarket white bec
 ome America’s dominant bread\, and how did rustic old-world bagels\, rye
 s\, and rolls find their way into our kitchens? Who was the early nineteen
 th-century dietary reformer who started the whole-grain revolution? Why no
 t knead? An enriching and enlightening cultural chronicle\, Andrew Coe ans
 wers these questions and more and offers carefully sourced historical reci
 pes to inspire the home baker.\n\nNote that this is not our usual 4th Sund
 ay meeting date\, it will be at 11:00. a.m on the 4th SATURDAY of the mont
 h.\nThe in-person presentation will take place at the historic City Colleg
 e\, Culinary Arts building in San Francisco and will include a guided tour
  of the facility after the lecture and tasting. It is easily accessible by
  BART\, a short walk from the Balboa Park station. Parking and building di
 rections instructions will be sent a few days before the event.\nAndrew Co
 e is an independent scholar and writer of many books including\, Pirate’
 s Gold: A Gilded Age Saga of Family\, Money and (Maybe) Murder\, and along
  with his wife\, Jane Ziegelman\, co-authors of A Square Meal: A Culinary 
 History of the Great Depression\, which won a James Beard award. His Chop 
 Suey: A Cultural History of Chinese Food in the United St...\n\n$10.00\n\n
 Tickets: https://www.facebook.com/events/1101160826182815/\nDetails: https
 ://sf.funcheap.com/american-bread-history-talk-tasting-guided-tour-sf/\nSo
 urce: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/11f.-W
 onder-Bread-Builds-Bodies.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T115902Z
LOCATION:City College\, 50 Frida Kahlo Way\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/american-bread-history-talk-tasting-guided-tou
 r-sf/
END:VEVENT
